{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_tcp_tcpsocketactor", "label": "TcpSocketActor", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/io/tcp.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Ausgehend \u2014 waehlt einen Remote-Host und besitzt genau eine Verbindung."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_tcp_tcpserveractor", "label": "TcpServerActor", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/io/tcp.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Eingehend \u2014 bindet einen lokalen Port und besitzt den Listener plus jede angenommene Verbindung. Baut auf derselben runtime-uebergreifenden TCP-Schicht auf wie der Cluster-Transport, TLS eingeschlossen."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_tcp_tcpframing", "label": "TcpFraming", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/io/tcp.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Framing ist eine Config-Union (bytes / lines / length-prefixed), keine Framer-Klasse zum Instanziieren. Beide Actors lesen dieselben Strategien aus demselben Code; auf dem Listener gilt das Framing pro angenommener Verbindung mit eigenem Re-Assembly-Buffer."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_tcp_framing_limit_enforcement", "label": "Frame-Limits und ihre Durchsetzung", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/io/tcp.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Ein Frame ueber seinem Limit wird nie gepuffert: die offenen Bytes werden verworfen und die Verbindung mit ihnen. maxLineLen begrenzt in Bytes inklusive der nicht terminierten Zeile \u2014 das ist die Haelfte, die den Re-Assembly-Buffer gegen einen Peer begrenzt, der nie einen Delimiter schickt. Ein leerer delimiter wird beim Start abgelehnt, weil er an jeder Position passt, ohne etwas zu verbrauchen."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_tcp_tcpservermessage", "label": "TcpServerMessage", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/io/tcp.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Eine kind-getaggte Union (connectionOpened / frame / connectionClosed) statt nackter Frames, weil ein Listener viele Verbindungen hat. Die Varianten sind einzeln importierbar. connectionClosed kommt bei jedem Ende \u2014 ein Signal, ein Codepfad."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_tcp_connection_id_addressing", "label": "Ein Actor, nicht einer pro Verbindung", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/io/tcp.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Verbindungen werden ueber eine opake connectionId adressiert, weil die Restart-Semantik eines Actors bei einem Socket nicht greift: ein neu gestarteter Verbindungs-Actor kann die TCP-Verbindung des Peers nicht wiederbeleben."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_tcp_tcp_server_tls", "label": "TLS ausliefern", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/io/tcp.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "tls traegt Zertifikats-Material (PEM/DER), niemals einen Pfad; ein halb konfiguriertes Credential wird beim Start abgelehnt statt still im Klartext zu binden. Fuer tls gibt es bewusst kein HOCON-Leaf \u2014 eine Config-Datei ist der falsche Ort fuer einen privaten Schluessel."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_tcp_maxconnections", "label": "maxConnections", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/io/tcp.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Eine Verbindung am Limit wird abgebrochen statt registriert \u2014 Abweisen an der Tuer. Abgebrochen, nicht geordnet beendet, weil ein FIN, das der Peer nie beantwortet, den Socket samt Dateideskriptor offen haelt."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_tcp_listener_outbound_buffer_zero", "label": "outboundBuffer ist beim Listener 0", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/io/tcp.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Puffern existiert, damit eine Nachricht einen Reconnect ueberlebt \u2014 beim Listener heisst getrennt aber, dass der Port unten ist und jede angenommene Verbindung ohnehin weg. Ein gepufferter Write benennt eine Id, die nie wiederkommt."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_tcp_tcp_gives_bytes_not_messages", "label": "TCP gibt Bytes, keine Nachrichten", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/io/tcp.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Ohne Framer muss Anwendungscode beliebige Byte-Grenzen wieder zusammensetzen \u2014 leicht falsch zu machen. Deshalb: nimm einen Framer, immer."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_tcp_no_connection_multiplexing", "label": "Kein Connection-Multiplexing", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/io/tcp.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Raw TCP ist Single-Stream pro Verbindung; bidirektional plus multiplexed heisst HTTP/2 (ueber gRPC) oder WebSocket."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_tcp_backpressure_not_automatic", "label": "Backpressure ist nicht automatisch", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/io/tcp.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fuellt sich der Kernel-Buffer, stauen sich nachfolgende Sends im Speicher. Fuer anhaltende Schreib-Workloads den Producer drosseln oder ein Protokoll mit eingebauter Flusskontrolle nehmen."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_tcp_when_tcp", "label": "Wann raw TCP", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/io/tcp.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Legacy-Protokolle, eigene Binaerprotokolle, Bruecken zu Nicht-HTTP-Services. Fuer neue Anwendungsprotokolle gilt: nicht zuerst zu raw TCP greifen \u2014 HTTP, WebSocket oder gRPC sind die besseren Startpunkte."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_tcp_tcpsocketactor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_tcp_tcpserveractor", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/io/tcp.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_tcp_tcpsocketactor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_tcp_tcpframing", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/io/tcp.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_tcp_tcpserveractor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_tcp_tcpframing", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/io/tcp.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_tcp_tcpserveractor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_tcp_tcpservermessage", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/io/tcp.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_tcp_tcpframing", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_tcp_framing_limit_enforcement", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/io/tcp.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_tcp_tcpserveractor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_tcp_tcp_server_tls", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/io/tcp.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_tcp_tcpserveractor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_tcp_maxconnections", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/io/tcp.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_tcp_connection_id_addressing", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_tcp_tcpserveractor", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/io/tcp.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_tcp_listener_outbound_buffer_zero", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_tcp_tcpserveractor", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/io/tcp.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_tcp_tcp_gives_bytes_not_messages", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_tcp_tcpframing", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/io/tcp.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_tcp_no_connection_multiplexing", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_tcp_tcpsocketactor", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/io/tcp.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_tcp_backpressure_not_automatic", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_tcp_tcpsocketactor", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/io/tcp.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_tcp_when_tcp", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_tcp_tcpsocketactor", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/io/tcp.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_tcp_tcpsocketactor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_overview_brokeractor", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/io/tcp.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_tcp_tcpserveractor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_overview_brokeractor", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/io/tcp.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_tcp_listener_outbound_buffer_zero", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_overview_outbound_buffer", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/io/tcp.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_tcp_tcpsocketactor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_udp_udpsocketactor", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/io/tcp.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_tcp_framing_limit_enforcement", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_overview_reconnect_with_backoff", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/co